00:00:05.510 --> 00:00:07.590 align:start position:0%
turkey is set to take a new step forward  in its quest to join the european union  at the general affairs council in  luxembourg on the 22nd of october  ministers are likely to confirm that  turkey can open a new chapter in its eu  accession negotiations  in all candidates must fulfill  requirements in 35 chapters or policy  areas so far turkey has opened 13.  the last chapter was opened more than  three years ago the council is also  expected to set a date for the accession  conference which will focus on chapter  22 regional policy and coordination of  structural instruments  turkey began its membership negotiations  in 2005.  the ministers will also discuss  preparations for the european council of  heads of state and government later in  the week  key items on the summit agenda include  the completion of the digital single  market youth unemployment and investment  as well as progress on strengthening  policies underpinning the euro single  currency and completing the banking  union  preparations for the eastern partnership  summit in lithuania at the end of next  month and the plight of asylum seekers  trying to cross the mediterranean to  europe will also be discussed  the ministers are also likely to endorse  a report on the european semester  process which helps member states to  better organize their budgets and  economic policies  the current cycle ended in july and the  next is due to commence in november when  the european commission publishes its  annual growth survey
 

